From 2c527e7f853389ae919a9a2ba715446bc064d26d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:52:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve execution-based review independence in
 neutral routing [daveey]

Canonical integration retains model attribution as audit provenance, permits same-model distinct review execution, and ignores historical concrete reviewer/strong-model restrictions. Genuine empty enabled registries, provider walls, quota episodes, preclaim cooldown and foreign-home no-write controls remain enforced.

Proof: integrated baseline18files391pass21fail; first reconciliation11files269pass3fail, final implementer-set51pass. Safety13files401pass1fail, final sharedblocker96pass. Shipped guidance regression failed on obsolete author-model exclusion before correction. Full scripts/check21green. No fleet remediation, deployment or exact-head review claimed.
